<div class=3D"journal-content-article " data-analytics-asset-id=3D"328417" =
data-analytics-asset-title=3D"FAQs on Health Insurance Regulations" data-an=
alytics-asset-type=3D"web-content">
=09

	<div class=3D"main">
    <section id=3D"faqContainer">
        <div class=3D"container-fluid">
            <div class=3D"row">
                <div class=3D"col-lg-11 section">
                    <div class=3D"row innerSection2">
                        <h4 class=3D"ml-3"><strong>FAQs</strong></h4>
						 <!--<a class=3D"accordion-expand-all" id=3D"expandCollapseAll" oncli=
ck=3D"expandAll();" href=3D"#">
						 + Expand All/Collapse All -
						 </a>-->
                    </div>
                    <div class=3D"mb-5">
                        <div class=3D"accordion" id=3D"accordionExample">
                                                    <div class=3D"card mb-0=
">
                                <div class=3D"card-header collapsed" id=3D"=
heading1" data-toggle=3D"collapse" data-target=3D"#collapse1" aria-expanded=
=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"collapse1">
                                    <h2 class=3D"mb-0">
                                        <strong>What is Health Insurance Bu=
siness?</strong>
                                    </h2>
                                    </div>
                                    <div id=3D"collapse1" class=3D"collapse=
 accordion-content" aria-labelledby=3D"heading1" data-parent=3D"#accordionE=
xample">
                                    <div class=3D"card-body">
                                        <p><span>Section 2 (6C) of Insuranc=
e Act, 1938 defines Health Insurance Business as under:<br>
"health insurance business" means the effecting of contracts which provide =
for sickness benefits or medical, surgical or hospital expense benefits, wh=
ether in-patient or out-patient travel cover and personal accident cover.<s=
pan> </span></span></p>
                                    </div>             =20
                                </div>               =20
                            </div>   =20
                            	           =20
                            <div class=3D"card mb-0">
                                <div class=3D"card-header collapsed" id=3D"=
heading2" data-toggle=3D"collapse" data-target=3D"#collapse2" aria-expanded=
=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"collapse2">
                                    <h2 class=3D"mb-0">
                                        <strong>Which Insurance Companies o=
ffer Health Insurance Policies in India?</strong>
                                    </h2>
                                    </div>
                                    <div id=3D"collapse2" class=3D"collapse=
 accordion-content" aria-labelledby=3D"heading2" data-parent=3D"#accordionE=
xample">
                                    <div class=3D"card-body">
                                        <p>Health Insurance policies are of=
fered by all Life, General and Health Insurance companies that are register=
ed with IRDAI. While General and Heath Insurance Companies offer both indem=
nity based and benefit based health insurance policies, Life Insurance Comp=
anies offer benefit based policies as per the extant Health Insurance Regul=
ations. All General and Health Insurance Companies also offer Personal Acci=
dent Policies, Domestic Travel Policies and Overseas Travel Policies. The n=
ames of the Insurance companies that are registered with IRDAI are availabl=
e in IRDAI website <a href=3D"http://www.irdai.gov.in/" target=3D"_blank">w=
ww.irdai.gov.in</a>.</p>
                                    </div>             =20
                                </div>               =20
                            </div>   =20
                            	           =20
                            <div class=3D"card mb-0">
                                <div class=3D"card-header collapsed" id=3D"=
heading3" data-toggle=3D"collapse" data-target=3D"#collapse3" aria-expanded=
=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"collapse3">
                                    <h2 class=3D"mb-0">
                                        <strong>What is the maximum age at =
entry for taking a Health Insurance policy? Whether Health Insurance is ava=
ilable lifelong once taken a policy?</strong>
                                    </h2>
                                    </div>
                                    <div id=3D"collapse3" class=3D"collapse=
 accordion-content" aria-labelledby=3D"heading3" data-parent=3D"#accordionE=
xample">
                                    <div class=3D"card-body">
                                        <p>In accordance to the provisions =
of Regulation 12(i) of IRDAI (Health Insurance) Regulations 2016 (HIR 2016)=
, all health insurance policies shall ordinarily provide for an entry age o=
f at least up to 65 years. There are also Health Insurance Products that of=
fer Health Insurance Coverage beyond age 65 years. In accordance to the pro=
visions of Regulation 12(ii) of HIR 2016,once a proposal is accepted in res=
pect of a health insurance policy (except Personal Accident and Travel Poli=
cies) and a policy is issued which is thereafter renewed periodically witho=
ut any break, further renewal shall not be denied on the grounds of age of =
the Insured. Thus, health insurance policies are lifelong renewable.</p>
                                    </div>             =20
                                </div>               =20
                            </div>   =20
                            	           =20
                            <div class=3D"card mb-0">
                                <div class=3D"card-header collapsed" id=3D"=
heading4" data-toggle=3D"collapse" data-target=3D"#collapse4" aria-expanded=
=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"collapse4">
                                    <h2 class=3D"mb-0">
                                        <strong>What is pre-existing diseas=
e?</strong>
                                    </h2>
                                    </div>
                                    <div id=3D"collapse4" class=3D"collapse=
 accordion-content" aria-labelledby=3D"heading4" data-parent=3D"#accordionE=
xample">
                                    <div class=3D"card-body">
                                        <p><span>As part of Guidelines on S=
tandardization, IRDAI has defined Pre-Existing Diseases (reproduced below i=
n verbatim), at Clause 33 of Chapter I of Guidelines on Standardization in =
Health Insurance under Sec 1 of IRDAI Master Circular ref IRDAI/HLT/REG/CIR=
/193/07/2020 dated 22.07.2020:<br>
Pre-existing Disease means any condition, ailment, injury or disease:<br>
a) That is/are diagnosed by a physician within 48 months prior to the effec=
tive date of the policy issued by the insurer or its reinstatement or&nbsp;=
<br>
b) For which medical advice or treatment was recommended by, or received fr=
om, a physician within 48 months prior to the effective date of the policy =
issued by the insurer or its reinstatement.<br>
(Life Insurers may define norms for applicability of PED at Reinstatement)<=
/span></p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
                                    </div>             =20
                                </div>               =20
                            </div>   =20
                            	           =20
                            <div class=3D"card mb-0">
                                <div class=3D"card-header collapsed" id=3D"=
heading5" data-toggle=3D"collapse" data-target=3D"#collapse5" aria-expanded=
=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"collapse5">
                                    <h2 class=3D"mb-0">
                                        <strong>Whether pre-existing diseas=
es are covered under a health insurance policy?</strong>
                                    </h2>
                                    </div>
                                    <div id=3D"collapse5" class=3D"collapse=
 accordion-content" aria-labelledby=3D"heading5" data-parent=3D"#accordionE=
xample">
                                    <div class=3D"card-body">
                                        <p>Offering health insurance covera=
ge to any person who has suffered / suffering from any disease / illness is=
 subject to underwriting policy and product design of an insurer. Insurers =
design products keeping in view certain factors such as viability and self-=
sustainability of products and the needs of the intended target market segm=
ent. Where a pre-existing disease(s) is disclosed and a health insurance po=
licy is granted, such pre-existing disease(s) shall be covered after a wait=
ing period as specified in the policy, which at the maximum shall not be ex=
ceeding 48 months.</p>

<p>However, in terms of Chapter IV of the Guidelines on Standardization of =
Exclusions in Health Insurance Contracts under Sec 1 of IRDAI Master Circul=
ar ref IRDAI/HLT/REG/CIR/193/07/2020 dated 22.07.2020, certain existing dis=
eases disclosed by the prospect are allowed to be permanently excluded.</p>
                                    </div>             =20
                                </div>               =20
                            </div>   =20
                            	           =20
                            <div class=3D"card mb-0">
                                <div class=3D"card-header collapsed" id=3D"=
heading6" data-toggle=3D"collapse" data-target=3D"#collapse6" aria-expanded=
=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"collapse6">
                                    <h2 class=3D"mb-0">
                                        <strong>Are there any principles on=
 charging premium for Health Insurance coverage?</strong>
                                    </h2>
                                    </div>
                                    <div id=3D"collapse6" class=3D"collapse=
 accordion-content" aria-labelledby=3D"heading6" data-parent=3D"#accordionE=
xample">
                                    <div class=3D"card-body">
                                        <p>IRDAI (Health Insurance) Regulat=
ions, 2016 at Regulation 10 have specified certain principles on pricing of=
 Health Insurance Products offered by Life, General and Health Insurers. Th=
ese principles are placed hereunder (in verbatim).</p>

<p><span><strong>Principles of Pricing of Health Insurance Products offered=
 by Life, General and Health Insurers:</strong><br>
a. Insurers shall ensure that the premium for a health insurance policy sha=
ll be based on,<br>
&nbsp; i. Age: for individual policies and group policies.<br>
&nbsp; ii. Other relevant risk factors as applicable<br>
b. For provision of cover under family floater, the impact of the multiple =
incidence of rates of all family members proposed to be covered shall be co=
nsidered.<br>
c. The premiums filed shall ordinarily be not changed for a period of three=
 years after a product has been cleared in accordance to the product filing=
 guidelines specified by the Authority. Thereafter the insurer may revise t=
he premium rates depending on the experience subject to (d) (e) and (f) her=
eunder. However, such revised rates shall not be changed for a further peri=
od of at least one year from the date of launching the revision.</span></p>
                                    </div>             =20
                                </div>               =20
                            </div>   =20
                            	           =20
                            <div class=3D"card mb-0">
                                <div class=3D"card-header collapsed" id=3D"=
heading7" data-toggle=3D"collapse" data-target=3D"#collapse7" aria-expanded=
=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"collapse7">
                                    <h2 class=3D"mb-0">
                                        <strong>Is any additional loading l=
evied / charged on premium?</strong>
                                    </h2>
                                    </div>
                                    <div id=3D"collapse7" class=3D"collapse=
 accordion-content" aria-labelledby=3D"heading7" data-parent=3D"#accordionE=
xample">
                                    <div class=3D"card-body">
                                        <p>In terms of Regulation 8(e) of t=
he IRDAI (Health Insurance) Regulations 2016, the insured shall be informed=
 in writing of any underwriting loading charged over and above the premium =
as filed with the Authority and specific consent for such loadings shall be=
 obtained before issuance of the policy.</p>
                                    </div>             =20
                                </div>               =20
                            </div>   =20
                            	           =20
                            <div class=3D"card mb-0">
                                <div class=3D"card-header collapsed" id=3D"=
heading8" data-toggle=3D"collapse" data-target=3D"#collapse8" aria-expanded=
=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"collapse8">
                                    <h2 class=3D"mb-0">
                                        <strong>Whether Premium rates are u=
nchanged?</strong>
                                    </h2>
                                    </div>
                                    <div id=3D"collapse8" class=3D"collapse=
 accordion-content" aria-labelledby=3D"heading8" data-parent=3D"#accordionE=
xample">
                                    <div class=3D"card-body">
                                        <p>The Premium rate shall be unchan=
ged for all group products and for all individual and family floater produc=
ts, other than travel insurance products, offered by General and Health Ins=
urers, for the term of the policy. For further information, Regulation 10 (=
d) (e) and (f) of IRDAI (Health Insurance) Regulations 2016 may be referred=
.</p>
                                    </div>             =20
                                </div>               =20
                            </div>   =20
                            	           =20
                            <div class=3D"card mb-0">
                                <div class=3D"card-header collapsed" id=3D"=
heading9" data-toggle=3D"collapse" data-target=3D"#collapse9" aria-expanded=
=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"collapse9">
                                    <h2 class=3D"mb-0">
                                        <strong>Whether health insurance pr=
emium can be collected by insurance company any number of days in advance?<=
/strong>
                                    </h2>
                                    </div>
                                    <div id=3D"collapse9" class=3D"collapse=
 accordion-content" aria-labelledby=3D"heading9" data-parent=3D"#accordionE=
xample">
                                    <div class=3D"card-body">
                                        <p>Premiums can be collected in adv=
ance maximum upto a period of 90 days before the renewal date.</p>
                                    </div>             =20
                                </div>               =20
                            </div>   =20
                            	           =20
                            <div class=3D"card mb-0">
                                <div class=3D"card-header collapsed" id=3D"=
heading10" data-toggle=3D"collapse" data-target=3D"#collapse10" aria-expand=
ed=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"collapse10">
                                    <h2 class=3D"mb-0">
                                        <strong>Who is Third Party Administ=
rator (TPA)?</strong>
                                    </h2>
                                    </div>
                                    <div id=3D"collapse10" class=3D"collaps=
e accordion-content" aria-labelledby=3D"heading10" data-parent=3D"#accordio=
nExample">
                                    <div class=3D"card-body">
                                        <p>Regulation 2(1)(m) of IRDAI (Thi=
rd Party Administrators =E2=80=93 Health Services) Regulations 2016, define=
s Third Party Administrator (TPA) as under:</p>

<p>=E2=80=9CThird Party Administrator (TPA)=E2=80=9D means a company regist=
ered with the Authority, and engaged by an insurer, for a fee or by whateve=
r name called and as may be mentioned in the health services agreement, for=
 providing health services as mentioned under these regulations.=E2=80=9D</=
p>
                                    </div>             =20
                                </div>               =20
                            </div>   =20
                            	           =20
                            <div class=3D"card mb-0">
                                <div class=3D"card-header collapsed" id=3D"=
heading11" data-toggle=3D"collapse" data-target=3D"#collapse11" aria-expand=
ed=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"collapse11">
                                    <h2 class=3D"mb-0">
                                        <strong>What is Cashless facility? =
Whether cashless facility is offered at all hospitals?</strong>
                                    </h2>
                                    </div>
                                    <div id=3D"collapse11" class=3D"collaps=
e accordion-content" aria-labelledby=3D"heading11" data-parent=3D"#accordio=
nExample">
                                    <div class=3D"card-body">
                                        <p>Cashless facility means a facili=
ty extended by the Insurer or Third Party Administrator (TPA) on behalf of =
the Insurer to the insured, where the payments for the costs of treatment u=
ndergone by the Insured in accordance with the policy terms and conditions,=
 are directly made to the network provider by the Insurer to the extent pre=
authorization is approved. Cashless facility shall be offered only at Netwo=
rk Providers which have entered into an agreement with the insurer to exten=
d such services.</p>
                                    </div>             =20
                                </div>               =20
                            </div>   =20
                            	           =20
                            <div class=3D"card mb-0">
                                <div class=3D"card-header collapsed" id=3D"=
heading12" data-toggle=3D"collapse" data-target=3D"#collapse12" aria-expand=
ed=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"collapse12">
                                    <h2 class=3D"mb-0">
                                        <strong>Whether reimbursement of cl=
aim can be availed for treatment taken at any hospital.</strong>
                                    </h2>
                                    </div>
                                    <div id=3D"collapse12" class=3D"collaps=
e accordion-content" aria-labelledby=3D"heading12" data-parent=3D"#accordio=
nExample">
                                    <div class=3D"card-body">
                                        <p>Reimbursement of a claim shall b=
e allowed at any hospital or medical establishment subject to the terms and=
 conditions of the policy contract. However such establishments must be lic=
ensed or registered as may be required by any Local, State or National Law =
as applicable.</p>
                                    </div>             =20
                                </div>               =20
                            </div>   =20
                            	           =20
                            <div class=3D"card mb-0">
                                <div class=3D"card-header collapsed" id=3D"=
heading13" data-toggle=3D"collapse" data-target=3D"#collapse13" aria-expand=
ed=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"collapse13">
                                    <h2 class=3D"mb-0">
                                        <strong>What is AYUSH Treatment? Wh=
ether AYUSH Treatment is allowed in all Health Insurance Policies?</strong>
                                    </h2>
                                    </div>
                                    <div id=3D"collapse13" class=3D"collaps=
e accordion-content" aria-labelledby=3D"heading13" data-parent=3D"#accordio=
nExample">
                                    <div class=3D"card-body">
                                        <p>AYUSH Treatment refers to the me=
dical and / or hospitalization treatments given under =E2=80=98Ayurveda, Yo=
ga and Naturopathy, Unani, Siddha and Homeopathy systems=E2=80=99.</p>

<p>Whether or not AYUSH treatment is allowed in a Health Insurance Policy i=
s subject to the product features offered by the insurers. The AYUSH treatm=
ent taken shall be covered as per the terms and conditions of policy contra=
ct.</p>
                                    </div>             =20
                                </div>               =20
                            </div>   =20
                            	           =20
                            <div class=3D"card mb-0">
                                <div class=3D"card-header collapsed" id=3D"=
heading14" data-toggle=3D"collapse" data-target=3D"#collapse14" aria-expand=
ed=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"collapse14">
                                    <h2 class=3D"mb-0">
                                        <strong>What is AYUSH Hospital?</st=
rong>
                                    </h2>
                                    </div>
                                    <div id=3D"collapse14" class=3D"collaps=
e accordion-content" aria-labelledby=3D"heading14" data-parent=3D"#accordio=
nExample">
                                    <div class=3D"card-body">
                                        <p>As part of Guidelines on Standar=
dization, IRDAI has defined AYUSH Hospital (reproduced below in verbatim), =
at clause 45 of Chapter I of Guidelines on Standardization in Health Insura=
nce under Sec 1 of IRDAI Master Circular ref IRDAI/HLT/REG/CIR/193/07/2020 =
dated 22.07.2020:</p>

<p>AYUSH Hospital:</p>

<p>An AYUSH Hospital is a healthcare facility wherein medical/surgical/para=
-surgical treatment procedures and interventions are carried out by AYUSH M=
edical Practitioner(s) comprising of any of the following:<br>
a. Central or State Government AYUSH Hospital; or<br>
b. Teaching hospital attached to AYUSH College recognized by the Central Go=
vernment/Central Council of Indian Medicine/Central Council for Homeopathy;=
 or<br>
c. AYUSH Hospital, standalone or co-located with in-patient healthcare faci=
lity of any recognized system of medicine, registered with the local author=
ities, wherever applicable, and is under the supervision of a qualified reg=
istered AYUSH Medical Practitioner and must comply with all the following c=
riterion:Medical Practitioner and must comply with all the following criter=
ion:<br>
&nbsp; i. Having at least 5 in-patient beds;<br>
&nbsp; ii. Having qualified AYUSH Medical Practitioner in charge round the =
clock;<br>
&nbsp; iii. Having dedicated AYUSH therapy sections as required and/or has =
equipped operation&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; theatre where s=
urgical procedures are to be carried out;<br>
&nbsp; iv. Maintaining daily records of the patients and making them access=
ible to the insurance&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; company=E2=
=80=99s authorized representative.</p>
                                    </div>             =20
                                </div>               =20
                            </div>   =20
                            	           =20
                            <div class=3D"card mb-0">
                                <div class=3D"card-header collapsed" id=3D"=
heading15" data-toggle=3D"collapse" data-target=3D"#collapse15" aria-expand=
ed=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"collapse15">
                                    <h2 class=3D"mb-0">
                                        <strong>What is AYUSH Day Care Cent=
re?</strong>
                                    </h2>
                                    </div>
                                    <div id=3D"collapse15" class=3D"collaps=
e accordion-content" aria-labelledby=3D"heading15" data-parent=3D"#accordio=
nExample">
                                    <div class=3D"card-body">
                                        <p>As part of Guidelines on Standar=
dization, IRDAI has defined AYUSH Hospital (reproduced below in verbatim), =
at clause 46 of Chapter I of Guidelines on Standardization in Health Insura=
nce under Sec 1 of IRDAI Master Circular ref IRDAI/HLT/REG/CIR/193/07/2020 =
dated 22.07.2020</p>

<p><span><strong>AYUSH Day Care Centre: </strong><br>
AYUSH Day Care Centre means and includes Community Health Centre (CHC), Pri=
mary Health Centre (PHC), Dispensary, Clinic, Polyclinic or any such health=
 centre which is registered with the local authorities, wherever applicable=
 and having facilities for carrying out treatment procedures and medical or=
 surgical/para-surgical interventions or both under the supervision of regi=
stered AYUSH Medical Practitioner (s) on day care basis without in-patient =
services and must comply with all the following criterion:<br>
i. Having qualified registered AYUSH Medical Practitioner(s) in charge;<br>
ii. Having dedicated AYUSH therapy sections as required and/or has equipped=
 operation theatre where surgical procedures are to be carried out;<br>
iii. Maintaining daily records of the patients and making them accessible t=
o the insurance company=E2=80=99s authorized representative.<br>
[Explanation: Medical Practitioner referred in the definition of =E2=80=9CA=
YUSH Hospital=E2=80=9D and =E2=80=9CAYUSH Day Care Centre=E2=80=9D shall ca=
rry the same meaning as defined in the definition of =E2=80=9CMedical Pract=
itioner=E2=80=9D under Chapter I of Guidelines]</span></p>
                                    </div>             =20
                                </div>               =20
                            </div>   =20
                            	           =20
                            <div class=3D"card mb-0">
                                <div class=3D"card-header collapsed" id=3D"=
heading16" data-toggle=3D"collapse" data-target=3D"#collapse16" aria-expand=
ed=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"collapse16">
                                    <h2 class=3D"mb-0">
                                        <strong>What are the Regulatory pro=
visions for settlement of Health Insurance claims by TPAs/Insurers?</strong=
>
                                    </h2>
                                    </div>
                                    <div id=3D"collapse16" class=3D"collaps=
e accordion-content" aria-labelledby=3D"heading16" data-parent=3D"#accordio=
nExample">
                                    <div class=3D"card-body">
                                        <p>Regulatory Provisions for settle=
ment of Health Insurance claims by Insurers/TPAs are mentioned below:</p>

<p><span>1) An insurer shall settle or reject a claim, within thirty days o=
f the receipt of the last =E2=80=98necessary=E2=80=99 document.<br>
2) Except in cases where a fraud is suspected, ordinarily no document not l=
isted in the policy terms and conditions shall be deemed =E2=80=98necessary=
=E2=80=99. The insurer shall also ensure that all the documents required fo=
r claims processing are called for at one time and that the documents are n=
ot called for in a piece-meal manner.<br>
3) Every Insurer may stipulate a period within which all necessary claim do=
cuments should be furnished by the policyholder/insured to make a claim. Ho=
wever, claims filed even beyond such period should be considered if there a=
re valid reasons for any delay.<br>
4) Every Insurance Claim shall be disposed of in accordance to the Terms an=
d Conditions of the policy contract and the extant Regulations governing th=
e settlement of Claims.<br>
5) Where a claim is denied or repudiated, the communication about the denia=
l or the repudiation shall be made only by the Insurer by specifically stat=
ing the reasons for the denial or repudiation, while necessarily referring =
to the corresponding policy conditions. The insurer shall also furnish the =
grievance redressal procedures available with the Insurance Company and wit=
h the Insurance Ombudsman along with the detailed addresses of the respecti=
ve offices.<br>
For further details please refer Regulation 26, 27 and 33 of IRDAI (Health =
Insurance) Regulations 2016.<br>
6) Further as per IRDAI (Protections of Policyholders=E2=80=99 Interests) R=
egulations 2017,<br>
a) In case of delay in payment of a claim, the insurer shall be liable to p=
ay interest from the date of receipt of last necessary document to the date=
 of payment of claim at a rate 2% above the bank rate.<br>
b) However, where circumstances of a claim warrant an investigation in the =
opinion of the insurer, it shall initiate and complete such investigation a=
t the earliest, in any case not later than 30 days from the date of receipt=
 of last necessary document. In such cases, Insurer shall settle the claim =
within 45 days from the date of receipt of last necessary document.<br>
(i) In case of delay beyond stipulated 45 days the Insurer shall be liable =
to pay interest at a rate 2% above the bank rate from the date of receipt o=
f last necessary document to the date of payment of claim.</span></p>
                                    </div>             =20
                                </div>               =20
                            </div>   =20
                            	           =20
                            <div class=3D"card mb-0">
                                <div class=3D"card-header collapsed" id=3D"=
heading17" data-toggle=3D"collapse" data-target=3D"#collapse17" aria-expand=
ed=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"collapse17">
                                    <h2 class=3D"mb-0">
                                        <strong>How Cost of pre-insurance h=
ealth checkup is treated by Life, General and Health Insurers:</strong>
                                    </h2>
                                    </div>
                                    <div id=3D"collapse17" class=3D"collaps=
e accordion-content" aria-labelledby=3D"heading17" data-parent=3D"#accordio=
nExample">
                                    <div class=3D"card-body">
                                        <p>The cost of any pre-insurance me=
dical examination shall generally form part of the expenses allowed in arri=
ving at the premium. However, in case of products with term of one year and=
 less, if such cost is to be incurred by the insured, not less than 50% of =
such cost shall be borne by the insurer once the proposal is accepted, exce=
pt in travel insurance policies.</p>
                                    </div>             =20
                                </div>               =20
                            </div>   =20
                            	           =20
                            <div class=3D"card mb-0">
                                <div class=3D"card-header collapsed" id=3D"=
heading18" data-toggle=3D"collapse" data-target=3D"#collapse18" aria-expand=
ed=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"collapse18">
                                    <h2 class=3D"mb-0">
                                        <strong>.If a person is having mult=
iple policies, are there any norms that specify the manner of settlement of=
 claims?</strong>
                                    </h2>
                                    </div>
                                    <div id=3D"collapse18" class=3D"collaps=
e accordion-content" aria-labelledby=3D"heading18" data-parent=3D"#accordio=
nExample">
                                    <div class=3D"card-body">
                                        <p><span>The norms on multiple poli=
cies are as under:<br>
i. In case of multiple policies which provide fixed benefits, on the occurr=
ence of the insured event in accordance with the terms and conditions of th=
e policies, each insurer&nbsp; shall make the claim payments independent of=
 payments received under other similar polices.<br>
ii. If two or more policies are taken by an insured during a period from on=
e or more insurers to indemnify treatment costs, the policyholder shall hav=
e the right to require a settlement of his/her claim in terms of any of his=
/her policies.<br>
1) In all such cases the insurer who has issued the chosen policy shall be =
obliged to settle the claim as long as the claim is within the limits of an=
d according to the terms of the chosen policy.<br>
2) Balance claim or claims disallowed under the earlier chosen policy/polic=
ies may be made from the other policy/policies even if the sum insured is n=
ot exhausted in the earlier chosen policy/policies. The insurer(s) in such =
cases shall independently settle the claim subject to the terms and conditi=
ons of other policy / policies so chosen.<br>
3) If the amount to be claimed exceeds the sum insured under a single polic=
y after considering the deductibles or co-pay, the policyholder shall have =
the right to choose insurers from whom he/she wants to claim the balance am=
ount.<br>
4) Where an insured has policies from more than one insurer to cover the sa=
me risk on indemnity basis, the insured shall only be indemnified the hospi=
talization costs in accordance with the terms and conditions of the chosen =
policy.</span></p>
                                    </div>             =20
                                </div>               =20
                            </div>   =20
                            	           =20
                            <div class=3D"card mb-0">
                                <div class=3D"card-header collapsed" id=3D"=
heading19" data-toggle=3D"collapse" data-target=3D"#collapse19" aria-expand=
ed=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"collapse19">
                                    <h2 class=3D"mb-0">
                                        <strong>Whether any proposal or med=
ical examination is required at renewal stage?</strong>
                                    </h2>
                                    </div>
                                    <div id=3D"collapse19" class=3D"collaps=
e accordion-content" aria-labelledby=3D"heading19" data-parent=3D"#accordio=
nExample">
                                    <div class=3D"card-body">
                                        <p>No Insurer shall resort to fresh=
 underwriting by calling for medical examination, fresh proposal form etc. =
at renewal stage where there is no change in Sum Insured offered.</p>
                                    </div>             =20
                                </div>               =20
                            </div>   =20
                            	           =20
                            <div class=3D"card mb-0">
                                <div class=3D"card-header collapsed" id=3D"=
heading20" data-toggle=3D"collapse" data-target=3D"#collapse20" aria-expand=
ed=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"collapse20">
                                    <h2 class=3D"mb-0">
                                        <strong>What is Copayment?</strong>
                                    </h2>
                                    </div>
                                    <div id=3D"collapse20" class=3D"collaps=
e accordion-content" aria-labelledby=3D"heading20" data-parent=3D"#accordio=
nExample">
                                    <div class=3D"card-body">
                                        <p>Co-payment means a cost sharing =
requirement under a health insurance policy that provides that the policyho=
lder/insured will bear a specified percentage of the admissible claims amou=
nt. A co-payment does not reduce the Sum Insured.</p>
                                    </div>             =20
                                </div>               =20
                            </div>   =20
                            	           =20
                            <div class=3D"card mb-0">
                                <div class=3D"card-header collapsed" id=3D"=
heading21" data-toggle=3D"collapse" data-target=3D"#collapse21" aria-expand=
ed=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"collapse21">
                                    <h2 class=3D"mb-0">
                                        <strong>What is Cumulative Bonus?</=
strong>
                                    </h2>
                                    </div>
                                    <div id=3D"collapse21" class=3D"collaps=
e accordion-content" aria-labelledby=3D"heading21" data-parent=3D"#accordio=
nExample">
                                    <div class=3D"card-body">
                                        <p>Cumulative Bonus means any incre=
ase or addition in the Sum Insured granted by the insurer without an associ=
ated increase in premium.</p>
                                    </div>             =20
                                </div>               =20
                            </div>   =20
                            	           =20
                            <div class=3D"card mb-0">
                                <div class=3D"card-header collapsed" id=3D"=
heading22" data-toggle=3D"collapse" data-target=3D"#collapse22" aria-expand=
ed=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"collapse22">
                                    <h2 class=3D"mb-0">
                                        <strong>What is deductible?</strong=
>
                                    </h2>
                                    </div>
                                    <div id=3D"collapse22" class=3D"collaps=
e accordion-content" aria-labelledby=3D"heading22" data-parent=3D"#accordio=
nExample">
                                    <div class=3D"card-body">
                                        <p>Deductible means a cost sharing =
requirement under a health insurance policy that provides that the insurer =
will not be liable for a specified rupee amount in case of indemnity polici=
es and for a specified number of days/hours in case of hospital cash polici=
es which will apply before any benefits are payable by the insurer. A deduc=
tible does not reduce the Sum Insured.</p>
                                    </div>             =20
                                </div>               =20
                            </div>   =20
                            	           =20
                            <div class=3D"card mb-0">
                                <div class=3D"card-header collapsed" id=3D"=
heading23" data-toggle=3D"collapse" data-target=3D"#collapse23" aria-expand=
ed=3D"true" aria-controls=3D"collapse23">
                                    <h2 class=3D"mb-0">
                                        <strong>What is Grace Period?</stro=
ng>
                                    </h2>
                                    </div>
                                    <div id=3D"collapse23" class=3D"collaps=
e accordion-content" aria-labelledby=3D"heading23" data-parent=3D"#accordio=
nExample">
                                    <div class=3D"card-body">
                                        <p>Grace period means the specified=
 period of time immediately following the premium due date during which a p=
ayment can be made to renew or continue a policy in force without loss of c=
ontinuity benefits such as waiting periods and coverage of preexisting dise=
ases. Coverage is not available for the period for which no premium is rece=
ived.</p>
                                    </div>             =20
                                </div>               =20
                            </div>   =20
                            	           =20
                    </div>

                    </div>
                =20
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>

